# StudioX Claw — .cursorrules
# Stack: Next.js 16 App Router + TypeScript 5 (existing) + Node.js 20 Gateway (new)

## IDENTITY AND SCOPE

You are working on StudioX Claw. Two distinct parts:
1. Existing Next.js 16 app (repo root) — DO NOT refactor or reorganize existing code
2. New Claw Gateway at /claw-gateway/ — Node.js 20 TypeScript service

Never mix: no Next.js imports in Gateway, no Gateway imports in Next.js.
When in /claw-gateway/: write Node.js code. When in /app/ or /components/: write Next.js.

## TYPESCRIPT RULES

- TypeScript strict mode is mandatory everywhere. Zero `any` types.
- Use `unknown` with type guards, or define proper interfaces.
- In /claw-gateway/ with NodeNext module resolution: all local imports must include .js extension.
  Correct:   import { ClawMessage } from './types/index.js'
  Incorrect: import { ClawMessage } from './types/index'
- All async functions must have typed return values (Promise<SpecificType>, not Promise<any>).
- Zod for all runtime validation of external input.

## NEXT.JS APP ROUTER RULES

- Server Components are the default. Add 'use client' only when interactivity requires it.
- Route handlers in app/api/ use the Web API Request/Response pattern (not Express).
- Never import firebase-admin in client components. Admin SDK is server-only.
- For auth in API routes: verify Firebase ID token server-side using Admin SDK.
- All new Claw pages: app/claw/. All new Claw API routes: app/api/claw/.
- New Claw UI components: components/claw/. Do not add to components/studio/.

## GATEWAY (NODE.JS) RULES

- Long-running process. In-memory state is valid (session store, connection maps).
- All channels extend BaseChannel from channels/base.ts.
- GatewayServer.routeMessage() is the SINGLE entry point for all channels.
- Channel adapters: protocol handling + immediate ack only. Business logic in agent/core.ts.
- Firebase Admin: initialized once in firebase-admin.ts, never re-initialized.

## TELEGRAM (grammY)

- Respond to webhooks within 3 seconds. Send "Got it! Generating..." immediately.
- Deliver generation results as separate messages via bot.api (not as replies to webhook).
- Use sendChatAction('upload_video' or 'upload_photo') while jobs are pending.
- Command handlers in commands.ts. Keyboard builders in keyboards.ts.
- Callback query data format: "action:jobId:userId" — validate userId match before processing.
- Unsubscribe Firestore listeners after 10 minutes.

## DISCORD (discord.js v14)

- Always call interaction.deferReply() before any async operation.
- Use interaction.editReply() for the final result, not followUp().
- EmbedBuilder for all rich responses. Never send raw text for generation results.
- ActionRowBuilder + ButtonBuilder for post-generation actions.
- Validate ButtonInteraction.user.id === original command user before processing.
- Slash commands defined in commands/index.ts. Register via register-commands.ts (not at startup).

## WEB CHAT (WebSocket)

- First message from client must be auth. Close 4001 if not.
- All WebSocket messages are JSON. No raw strings.
- Keepalive: ping every 30 seconds. Close if no pong within 10 seconds.
- Use Firebase Admin auth.verifyIdToken() — never trust client-provided UID.

## SKILL SYSTEM RULES

- Every skill is a SKILL.md file with YAML frontmatter parsed by gray-matter.
- Required fields: name, description, version, author, triggers[], args[], cost_estimate, channels[], agent.
- Skills are DATA — never eval() or Function() skill content.
- SkillExecutor reads credit balance LIVE from Firestore before every execution. No exceptions.
- Credit check is mandatory for every skill. No bypasses, not even in admin/test paths.
- SkillRegistry.findByTrigger() uses longest-match against triggers array.

## MEMORY SYSTEM RULES

- UserMemory stored in Firestore at claw_memory/{firebaseUID}.
- SessionContext is in-memory only (Map, TTL 30 minutes).
- injectMemoryIntoPrompt() enriches prompts before every generation.
- New users get default values — never throw or return null for first-time users.
- SOUL.md and IDENTITY.md read at Gateway startup. Not user-editable.

## PAIRING SYSTEM RULES

- Codes: crypto.randomInt(100000, 999999). Never Math.random().
- Codes expire in 10 minutes. Single-use only.
- approvePairing() throws typed PairingError: 'not_found' | 'expired' | 'already_used'.
- LinkResolver called on EVERY inbound message. If null for DM: prompt to pair.
- Never expose Firebase UIDs in channel messages.
- Return 401 (not 403) for unauthenticated requests to Claw API routes.

## CREDIT SYSTEM RULES

- Source of truth: Firestore users/{uid}.tokenBalance
- Pattern: read balance → compare cost → if ok: proceed + deduct → else: return error
- Every channel response must include: "X credits used | Balance: Y credits"
- Credit low alert: 500cr threshold, max once per 24h per user.
- Never mock credit balances in production code paths.

## SCHEDULER RULES

- Three formats: { at: ISO }, { every: "2h" }, { cron: "0 9 * * MON", timezone }
- Validate timezone with Intl.supportedValuesOf('timeZone').
- Persist all jobs in Firestore. rehydrateJobs() on Gateway restart.
- Failed jobs: retry 3x at 5-min intervals, then permanently_failed + notify.
- Heartbeat tasks catch own errors. Never crash the Gateway.

## SECURITY RULES

- Never log: bot tokens, Firebase private keys, credit balances, Firebase UIDs.
- All user input validated with Zod before use.
- WhatsApp Baileys: mark all code with comments noting unofficial API.
- OWASP: parameterize all Firestore queries, validate all inputs.

## ANTI-PATTERNS — NEVER DO THESE

- Never cross-import between Next.js app and claw-gateway
- Never Math.random() for security-sensitive randomness
- Never eval() or new Function() with skill content
- Never await long operations before sending channel ack
- Never skip the credit check for any generation
- Never add Claw features to existing studio components
- Never use polling for Telegram (webhook only in production)
- Never call interaction.reply() after deferReply() — use editReply()

## FILE NAMING

- Gateway source: camelCase.ts (connectionManager.ts)
- Gateway skills: kebab-case.md (image-gen.md, template-fire-lava.md)
- Next.js components: PascalCase.tsx (SkillCard.tsx, WebChatWidget.tsx)
- Identity files: UPPERCASE.md (SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md, MEMORY.md)
- Test files: kebab-case.test.ts (message-routing.test.ts)

## COMMIT FORMAT

claw(scope): description

Scopes: gateway, telegram, discord, slack, whatsapp, web-chat, skills,
        memory, scheduler, pairing, marketplace, tests

Examples:
  claw(telegram): add async video delivery with Firestore onSnapshot
  claw(skills): implement smart-model-picker credit optimization
  claw(pairing): enforce 10-minute code expiry with crypto.randomInt
  claw(web-chat): add WebSocket keepalive ping/pong
